# Trivy ignore list.
#
# Every entry must state why the vulnerability is not reachable in this
# deployment and carry a review date. Entries without a justification do not
# belong here — the blocking CRITICAL/HIGH gate in .github/workflows/ci.yml is
# only worth having if the exceptions are deliberate and few.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 — react-router: RSC Mode CSRF Bypass Allows Action
# Execution Before 400 Response.
#
# Present: react-router 7.18.2 (transitive, via react-router-dom in apps/web).
# Fixed in: 8.3.0 — a major version bump with breaking routing API changes.
#
# Not reachable here. The advisory applies to React Server Components mode,
# which requires a server-side router runtime. apps/web is a client-side SPA
# built by Vite and served as static assets by nginx; there is no RSC runtime,
# no server-side router, and no router action handling in the deployed
# artifact. The API is NestJS and does not use react-router at all.
#
# CSRF protection for state-changing requests is enforced server-side by the
# API's auth guard and bearer-token scheme, not by the router.
#
# Action: upgrade react-router-dom to v8 as planned work, outside the
# competition deadline, with routing regression testing across the customer
# PhoneShell and ops console shells.
#
# Review by: 2026-09-30
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2
